post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
legion-powerctl writes volatile CPU SMU power limits through RyzenAdj.
Use at your own risk. Not affiliated with Lenovo, AMD, or CachyOS;
Legion is a trademark of Lenovo.

The package itself enables nothing. Boot persistence comes from:

    legion-powerctl doctor
    sudo legion-powerctl enable    # runs doctor first; --force skips the gate

(./install.sh runs this enable step for you unless --no-enable was given.)
Fire Range / HX CPUs need ryzenadj 0.19.0 or newer.
EOF
}

pre_remove() {
    systemctl disable --now legion-powerctl.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'EOF'
If you edited the bundled profiles, check for .pacnew files under
/etc/legion-powerctl. Reapply the active profile with:

    sudo legion-powerctl apply
EOF
}
